Luis J. Tosina Fernández is a professor at Universidad de Extremadura, 
Spain, where he obtained his PhD in 2016 with a proposal for a universal sys-
tem for the classification of proverbs. His research interest lies within the fields 
of paremiology and folklore, particularly in relation to the use of proverbs in 
present-day media and how these contribute to the spread of paremiology. He 
has published several papers on this topic as well as in relation to some socio-
political uses of paremiology. He has also presented his research at various 
international conferences, particularly at the Interdisciplinary Colloquium on 
Proverbs, organized by the International Association of Paremiology, of which 
he is an associate and the secretary of the International Council.
